From: ai-hakzarov <226896199+ai-hakzarov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:31:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] 9759: Decompiler: a piece or zero extension of a laned
 register that is not a lane size suggests the lane size that tiles it

ActionLaneDivide::collectLaneSizes only registered a lane size when a SUBPIECE
output or a PIECE input had exactly an allowed lane size, so a 12-byte piece of
a 16-byte vector register (three floats of a four-float vector, taken as one
piece) suggested nothing, and in mode 2 the default 8-byte lanes failed on it:
the function kept the whole register and printed the piece as a byte array with
lane extractions. Such a piece now registers the largest allowed lane size that
tiles both the piece and its offset within the register, provided the piece
holds at least two such lanes (12 bytes at offset 0 gives 4).

A vector whose top lane is cleared by shuffling against a zero register is
simplified into a zero extension of its low three lanes; the extended value
had no reader or definition suggesting a lane size, so only the default lane
size was tried and failed. The input of a defining INT_ZEXT now registers the
lane size that tiles it when the input is not itself a lane size; a single
extended lane still suggests nothing.

The datatest zerotop.xml builds such a vector with two shuffles against a
zero register and stores it whole; the top lane must print as a float, not as
an extraction from a byte array.
